<scopecontent encodinganalog="520$a">
<head>Scope and Content
</head>
<p>Collection consists of legal documents, memorabilia, two photographs, and some correspondence.
</p>
</scopecontent>

<arrangement encodinganalog="351">
<head>Arrangement
</head>
<p>The collection is arranged alphabetically and chronologically. It is boxed with MS-728 and MS-731.</p>

<p>f. 1: Accession folder</p>

<p>f. 2: Crank, Richard G. Will, 1881</p>

<p>f. 3: Huff, James W. and Sarah - Deeds [of properties in Albemarle Co.], 1871-1891</p>

<p>f. 4: Huff Family Memorabilia - correspondence and War Ration Books, 1906, [1928-1929], n.d.</p>

<p>f. 5: Judgment Docket Book, 1855-1900</p>

<p>f. 6: Ledger, 1884-1890</p>

<p>f. 7: Memorabilia - "A Call to Prayer. Devotions during the Period of The Invasion and the repeated use as the conflict deepens," [endorsed by the Forward Movement]. Cincinnati, OH., n.d.; University of Virginia - The Hospital, n.d.</p>

<p>f. 8: Photographs:</p>

<p>1. Tobacco field at Oak Lawn, Earlysville, VA, 1899</p>

<p>2. Group of women, n.d.</p>

<p>3. Two men, n.d.</p>

<p>4. "Front and side piazzas at Goodmar [?]," n.d.</p>

<p>f. 9: State of Virginia Legal Forms: Report of Commission Regarding the Insanity, Form No. 146 (190_); Warrant of Arrest, State of Virginia, County of Albemarle (189_)</p>

<p>f. 10: [Twyman, Jos. W.] Notebooks [with accounts, recipes], 1833, 1890
</p>
</arrangement>

